---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const deletionSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "IDSnap Account & Data Deletion Instructions",
  "description": "Official Data Deletion policy for IDSnap as required by Google Play Store policies. Explains our accountless, local storage model and instant wipe procedures.",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "IDSnap",
    "url": "https://idsnap.app"
  }
};
---

<Layout
  title="Account & Data Deletion Policy (Google Play Compliance)"
  description="How to delete your data from IDSnap. Because IDSnap keeps your documents only on your phone, you have total and immediate control over wiping your records."
  schema={deletionSchema}
>
  <div class="container legal-page-container">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <div class="badge-pill">
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <polyline points="3 6 5 6 21 6"></polyline>
          <path d="M19 6v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6m3 0V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2"></path>
        </svg>
        Google Play Store Compliance
      </div>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Account & Data Deletion Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">In compliance with Google Play Developer Policy on User Data & Account Deletion</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Overview Banner -->
    <div class="card-glass summary-box">
      <h3>No Accounts and No Document Servers</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>IDSnap does not have user accounts or logins, and never uploads your documents.</strong> We do not store your name, documents, photos, or 2FA keys on any server. (The ads in the app are provided by Google, which may use your device's advertising ID: you can reset or delete it in your phone's settings, and change your ad choices in the app under Settings → Ad privacy choices.) Because 100% of your data resides locally on your physical phone, you do not need to submit a ticket, wait for an administrator, or verify your email to delete your data. You possess instant, sovereign control over your data deletion at all times.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>How to Delete Your Data</h2>
        <p>You can permanently delete your data using any of the following methods:</p>

        <div class="deletion-steps-grid">
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">Method 1</div>
            <h3>Delete Individual Files or 2FA Accounts In-App</h3>
            <p>
              Open IDSnap $\rightarrow$ navigate to the file or 2FA entry $\rightarrow$ swipe or tap the three dots $\rightarrow$ tap <strong>Delete</strong>.
            </p>
            <p class="step-sub">
              The file is immediately unlinked and its physical bytes on the local storage partition are overwritten and erased.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">Method 2</div>
            <h3>Wipe All App Data via Device Settings (Instant Total Wipe)</h3>
            <p>
              To delete all documents, ID cards, 2FA keys, drafts, and database entries at once without uninstalling:
            </p>
            <ol class="steps-list">
              <li>Open your phone's <strong>Settings</strong> app.</li>
              <li>Tap <strong>Apps</strong> or <strong>Application Manager</strong>.</li>
              <li>Select <strong>IDSnap</strong>.</li>
              <li>Tap <strong>Storage & Cache</strong> $\rightarrow$ tap <strong>Clear Storage / Clear Data</strong>.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="step-sub">
              This completely erases the local SQLite database, KeyStore entries, and application sandbox.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-num">Method 3</div>
            <h3>Uninstall the Application</h3>
            <p>
              Press and hold the IDSnap app icon on your home screen or app drawer, and tap <strong>Uninstall</strong>.
            </p>
            <p class="step-sub">
              The mobile operating system (Android / iOS) automatically destroys the app's sandboxed storage directory, eliminating 100% of all files, keys, and configurations.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Data Retention Period</h2>
        <p>
          Since IDSnap never transmits your documents, their retention period on our side is <strong>Zero (0) days</strong>: once you delete a file or uninstall the app, it is gone. There are no backups, snapshots, or logs containing your documents on any remote server.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Need Assistance?</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding data storage or wish to verify our on-device architecture, reach out to our team:
        </p>
        <div class="contact-box">
          <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@idsnap.app">support@idsnap.app</a></p>
          <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Data Deletion Inquiry</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-container {
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .legal-title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }

  .summary-box {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    background-color: var(--surface-container-high);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
  }

  .summary-box h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--on-surface);
  }

  .summary-box p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--on-surface);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--outline-variant);
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .deletion-steps-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .step-card {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .step-num {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary);
    background-color: var(--primary-container);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .step-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .steps-list {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .step-sub {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .contact-box {
    background-color: var(--surface-container);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
